## Executive Summary

Lemniscate has a **strong existing security posture**. A prior hardening pass established API key authentication, CSRF protection, CSP with nonces, rate limiting, upload validation, environment variable enforcement, and Docker hardening. This audit found **no critical vulnerabilities**, **no hardcoded secrets**, and **0 npm vulnerabilities**.

Eight (8) improvements were identified and implemented, ranging from a HIGH severity timing attack fix to LOW severity consistency improvements. All changes are backward-compatible and covered by tests.

