## Phase 6: File Upload Security

### Status: ✅ STRONG (one fix applied)

**Existing controls:**
- MIME type allowlist (PDF, DOCX, DOC, TXT, MD)
- Extension allowlist (cross-checked with MIME)
- Magic byte validation for PDF, DOCX
- UTF-8 content validation for text files (rejects NULL bytes, excessive control chars)
- Filename sanitization (strips control chars, path separators, `..`, RTL override chars)
- Path traversal defense in storage layer (`uploadPath()` boundary check)
- File size limit (25 MB)
- Content hash deduplication (SHA-256)
- Concurrent upload race condition handling (P2002 catch)

### Finding 6.1 — Missing `.doc` Magic Byte Validation [MEDIUM] ✅ FIXED

**Before:** The `.doc` extension was accepted but `validateMagicBytes()` had no check for it — it fell through to `return true`. A `.txt` file renamed to `.doc` would pass validation.

**After:** Added OLE2/CFBF magic byte check: `D0 CF 11 E0 A1 B1 1A E1` (8 bytes). Also changed the default fallthrough from `return true` to `return false` — unknown extensions are now rejected instead of accepted.

**Files changed:** `src/app/api/documents/upload/route.ts`  
**Tests added:** `src/__tests__/security/upload-validation.test.ts` (4 new cases)

