## Phase 9: Infrastructure Hardening

### Status: ✅ GOOD (one fix applied)

**Existing controls:**
- Multi-stage Dockerfile (build deps never ship to runtime)
- Non-root user (`nextjs:nodejs`, uid 1001)
- `no-new-privileges` security option in docker-compose
- `apk update && apk upgrade` in both Dockerfiles
- `--ignore-scripts` on npm/bun install (prevents lifecycle script attacks)
- Worker port internal-only (not exposed externally)
- Caddy request body limit (30 MB)
- Health checks on all services
- Named volumes for database and uploads (persistent across restarts)
- Automated SQLite backup scheduler with retention

### Finding 9.1 — Missing HSTS in Caddyfile [LOW] ✅ FIXED

**Before:** Caddy did not set HSTS header (Next.js set it, but the reverse proxy should too for defense-in-depth).

**After:** Added `Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains"` to Caddyfile.

**Files changed:** `Caddyfile`

