## Phase 10: Security Headers

### Status: ✅ GOOD (one fix applied)

**Existing headers (Next.js + Caddy):**
- `Content-Security-Policy` with per-request nonce
- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`
- `X-Frame-Options: DENY`
- `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`
- `Strict-Transport-Security` (Next.js + Caddy)
- `Permissions-Policy` (camera, microphone, geolocation, payment disabled)
- `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin`
- `Cache-Control: no-store` on API routes
- Server identification removed by Caddy

### Finding 10.1 — CSP Allows Unencrypted WebSocket and Missing Directives [MEDIUM] ✅ FIXED

**Before:** CSP `connect-src` included `ws:` (unencrypted WebSocket) in all environments. Missing `object-src 'none'` and `base-uri 'self'`.

**After:**
- Production: `connect-src 'self' wss:` (encrypted only)
- Development: `connect-src 'self' ws: wss:` (allows local HMR)
- Added `object-src 'none'` (blocks Flash/plugins/Java applets)
- Added `base-uri 'self'` (prevents `<base>` tag injection)

**Files changed:** `src/proxy.ts`  
**Tests added:** `src/__tests__/security/csp.test.ts` (2 new cases)

